  "membership_hash": "SHA256 of compact JSON sorted numeric [game_id,event_id] pairs; no dates or outcomes in digest",
  "design": "Original calibration later-half calendar blocks only, including partial first month. Fixed model is saved earlier-half conditional map; expanding model uses all calibration rows strictly earlier than each test block's first date. First block reuses identical saved map for both outputs; no redundant fit. Never fit raw movement model, shooter effects or global-only adjustment.",
  "preflight": "Both folds and every planned block before ANY fit: exact source closure and identity/date/outcome joins; model/schema/settings unchanged; planned event/game counts, dates and key hashes exact; each training stage >=100 events and >=30 games and both outcomes; nonempty test stage with sparse periods retained and flagged, not repaired; raw train end earlier than calibration start; training/test game and date disjoint; original numerical/resource bounds. Fail rather than alter the plan.",
  "inference": "Saved raw model only; fixed calibration probabilities exactly replay prior calibration-identity-inputs. New maps JSON roundtrip and independent scalar parity <=1e-12; complete finite interior output arrays, batch reversal and singleton parity; source and output hashes rechecked after execution.",
  "guard": "Each fold aggregate over all planned later-half events: expanding Brier <= fixed Brier AND expanding log loss <= fixed log loss, strict point comparison without tolerance. Both folds must pass. Monthly and subgroup results are diagnostics, not selectors. No automatic acceptance even if guard passes.",
  "limitations": [
    "Adaptive development motivated by inspected outer validation; this is not an untouched superiority test.",
    "Earlier fold validation overlaps later fold calibration historically, so these cohorts are not newly blinded. Outcomes may have been seen in previous tasks.",
    "Integrity verification/reuse may read outer artifact bytes; outer validation rows/outcomes are not inputs to this study's fitting, scoring, or policy selection.",
    "Rolling expanding history changes support and recency jointly; not a causal separation of those factors.",
    "Intervals condition on fixed fitted maps and omit fitting, serial dependence beyond games, and model-selection uncertainty.",
    "No parameter/split search, probability-band tuning, identity adjustment or new data download.",
    "No neutral-xG replacement, production, daily finishing, uncertainty, GAR or FPAR acceptance."
  ]
